<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jacinto Canek</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1731–<a href="/years/1761">1761</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jacinto Canek was a Maya leader who led an uprising against Spanish rule at Cisteil in Yucatán in November 1761. Taking the name of the last Itza kings, he was proclaimed king by his followers, but Spanish forces crushed the revolt within days. He was tortured and executed in Mérida in December 1761, and he is remembered as a symbol of Maya resistance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jacinto-canek.jpg" alt="Jacinto Canek" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yodigo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jacinto_Canek.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
